From 0868d038b14ea078dc0eb6a86c3544cdf6c481d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chris <08a487@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:28:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] arm64: Let CPUs left offline at boot be brought online
 later

With the spin-table enable method a CPU can't be taken offline, so arm64
registered such CPUs as not hotpluggable, and their sysfs online attribute
was read-only. A CPU kept offline at boot (maxcpus=) could then never be
started, even though spin-table can boot it at any time: MSM8994 firmware
without PSCI powers its cores up after boot (msm8994-cpu-boot), into the
spin table. Let those CPUs be onlined; offlining them still fails in
op_cpu_disable().
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c
index 29c6100f0..7b2a70747 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c
@@ -388,7 +388,12 @@ static inline bool cpu_can_disable(unsigned int cpu)
 
 bool arch_cpu_is_hotpluggable(int num)
 {
-	return cpu_can_disable(num);
+	/*
+	 * A CPU left offline at boot (maxcpus=) can still be brought online
+	 * later, even when its enable method can't take it down again
+	 * (spin-table): offlining it then fails cleanly in op_cpu_disable().
+	 */
+	return cpu_can_disable(num) || !cpu_online(num);
 }
 
 static void dump_kernel_offset(void)
